"why": "The sentence explains the gap between the folklore and the industry-wide findings described before [2] as an artefact of selection, which the next sentence then corrects for (‘Correcting for this bias…’). [3] is tempting because survivorship seems another reason pioneers look better than they are, but the sentence before it would then correct a bias that had not yet been identified."
