"why": "‘Therefore’ draws on the physicists’ demonstration before [3] that Wegener’s forces were far too weak, turning it into a defence of the sceptics. [4] is tempting because the defence fits the episode’s moral, but there ‘therefore’ would follow Wegener’s vindication rather than the objection, and it would separate ‘wrong about how it occurred’ from the sentence that explains it."
