"why": "The sentence names the two parties to the ‘contest’ announced in the first sentence—sediment building the land, compaction and waves wearing it away—so that the next sentence can say that ‘supply outran loss’. [3] is the most tempting, because the dams and levees that follow concern sediment and the sentence seems to describe the balance that has just shifted; but by then ‘supply’, ‘loss’, and ‘the other side’ would already have been used with nothing in the paragraph for them to refer to."
